{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "instructions",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 210,
      "text": "## Diagram editing playground\n\nClick a shape to see its Inspector properties. Try the alignment segments, line style and independent fill and outline colors. Double-click a shape to edit its text.\n\nCtrl-click several shapes, then drag them together. Click the background to inspect diagram settings. Try a background color, then Theme Default.\n\nSelect a connector and drag either tip to a new shape, into a shape's center for automatic anchoring, or onto empty space. Move the attached shape and watch the connector follow.",
      "yavc": { "shape": "text" }
    },
    {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 30,
      "y": 270,
      "width": 150,
      "height": 80,
      "text": "Start\nCentered by default",
      "color": "4",
      "yavc": { "shape": "oval" }
    },
    {
      "id": "process",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 250,
      "y": 270,
      "width": 180,
      "height": 80,
      "text": "Process\nExplicitly centered",
      "color": "5",
      "yavc": { "shape": "rounded", "textAlign": "center", "textVerticalAlign": "middle" }
    },
    {
      "id": "decision",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 490,
